maya: Heads-up — I built a minimal repro for Bun + Deno weirdness with the Redwood JS SDK in edge mode. Auth header gets dropped on the retry path. :thinking_face:

sam: Oh interesting, repro please? :eyes:

maya: Paste below. basically: import the SDK via ESM in Deno (import_map) and Bun ends up loading the CJS entry. On a 401 retry we re-call fetch but the Authorization header disappears.

maya: ```json
// import_map.json
{
  "imports": {
    "@redwood/inference": "./node_modules/@redwood/inference/dist/esm/index.js"
  }
}
```

maya: And the retry helper is basically:```js
async function retryFetch(url, opts) {
  const res = await fetch(url, opts);
  if (res.status === 401) {
    // refresh token and retry
    const token = await refreshToken();
    opts.headers = { ...opts.headers, Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` };
    return fetch(url, opts); // second call loses headers in Bun/Deno fallback
  }
  return res;
}
```

jonah: Can you paste the actual stack/observed headers from the failing run? Bun or Deno?

maya: Reprobed on both. In Bun v1.1.x the second fetch shows no Authorization header in the request inspector. In Deno (edge runtime env) the fetch polyfill used in our test harness clones Request badly. The server logs show Authorization missing on retry.

li: Quick thought: many runtimes implement `fetch` such that reusing the same Headers object or Request can mutate/clear it when consumed. Workaround is to always make a fresh Request or clone headers with `new Headers(old)`. Example:```js
const safeHeaders = new Headers(opts.headers || {});
safeHeaders.set('Authorization', `Bearer ${token}`);
return fetch(url, { ...opts, headers: safeHeaders });
```

sam: Good call. Could be conditional-exports + loader resolution path causing a different helper to be used (node vs edge utils). We should ensure SDK always uses a tiny internal header-clone utility under edge builds.

maya: I also noticed our bundler shim for Bun does `globalThis.fetch = (p, o) => nativeFetch(new Request(p, o))` which can consume streams/headers. If we switch to `return nativeFetch(p, { ...o, headers: new Headers(o?.headers) })` it seems more robust.

devex-bot: Issue created: RED-DEVEX-472 - "edge: preserve headers on retry across runtimes" (assigned to @maya).

infra-bot: PR opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/pull/839 — adds header-clone util + unit tests for Bun/Deno fetch retry. CI: linux, mac, deno. :rocket:

sam: Nice. Can we add a tiny loader in the ESM build that exports `cloneHeaders` and make all retry paths import it? Keeps conditional exports minimal.

jonah: Add an integration test that runs the repro under Bun and Deno (via deno task) and asserts the Authorization header arrives on the second call. Maybe run in CI as optional matrix.

maya: I'll add the test and a fallback in the edge build. I'll also add a short note in the SDK CHANGELOG under "compatibility fixes". Ping me for review, @sam.

li: Thanks for the repro — saved a bunch of time. :+1:

maya: Filed PR draft and linked the repro and server logs in the PR description. Planning to land after tests.

sam: sweet, thanks everyone.
